CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772659301
OL,1,Vk4                               G7/19
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGVIOLENCE FLARES AT
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGLIVERPOOL MATCH
OL,4,D
OL,5, Italian riot police have separated
OL,6, fighting Liverpool and Genoa football
OL,7, fans before tonight's UEFA Cup match.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FA group of around 70 Genoa supporters
OL,10,Fcharged Liverpool fans as they arrived
OL,11,Fat the Luigi Ferraris stadium. Sticks
OL,12,Fand iron bars were used as weapons.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FBottles were thrown at the Liverpool
OL,15,Ffans as they were then escorted by
OL,16,Fabout 100 police officers to join the
OL,17,Fother 1,600 Liverpool supporters there.
OL,19,FThe match is the first competitive game
OL,20,Fbetween Liverpool and an Italian side
OL,21,Fsince the 1985 Heysel stadium disaster.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG04-03-92F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
